SCARPACCIA 

Originally this recipe calls for a mix of all purpose flour, chickpea flour / cornmeal flour but I’ve used only chickpea flour. Also you can swap the zucchini for other veggies (like bell pepper, leeks, onions).  

INGREDIENTS  

125gr chickpea flour  

325ml water, room temperature  

25ml high quality olive oil 

1 medium zucchini (roughly 150gr), thinly sliced 

1 small red onion, sliced  

25gr mixed seeds (e.g. hemp seeds, chia seeds, sunflower seeds, sesame seeds) 

Salt  

Black ground pepper  

COMPLETE THE DISH 

Side of salad  

METHOD 

In a bowl whisk together flour and water making sure all the lumps and the surface bubbles are removed (use a spoon to remove them). Ideally you would leave it to rest overnight but if you are in a hurry you can just let it rest for 1 hour.  

Meanwhile preheat your oven to 200C and line a baking tray with baking paper. 

Add the raw chopped veggies to the mixture along with the oil and salt.  

Pour the mixture on the baking tray, level it with a spatula. Sprinkle the seeds on top, add a pinch of pepper and bake for 40 minutes or until the top is golden.  

Serve with a side of salad  

